Title: AROS: Workbench start and the GUI_RENDERER ToolType
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: Started from Workbench (argc 0, argv = WBStartup) LibreSprite would read the WBStartup message as argv, could not open the files of project icons, and its console output opened a CON: window; there was no way to choose the renderer per installation as in other AROS programs.
Change: main.cpp: on Workbench start build argv from the WBStartup icons (paths in UTF-8) and send stdout/stderr to NIL:. app/aros_gui_renderer.cpp: the GUI_RENDERER ToolType of the program icon: CPU without OpenGL, GPU with OpenGL, AUTO (default) OpenGL when gl.library 20 opens and the GPU acceleration preference is on; the choice is logged.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: local-only
Verification: mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16: --verbose log "GUI_RENDERER=AUTO, gl.library present: OpenGL" with the AUTO icon and "GUI_RENDERER=CPU ... CPU" with a CPU icon; double-click on a project icon (default tool LibreSprite) opened that PNG, no CON: window; after quitting, Status lists no LibreSprite process. Also: after an OpenGL run, the redirected log could be deleted and later Shell redirection worked (no files left in use).
Removal: AROS-specific.
